{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-roadtypes-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d, the ROAD TYPE dimension: the `expand-roadtypes` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm` -- Washtenaw, August, weekday 6am, passenger cars on four fuels, Total Energy Consumption at running and start exhaust, on ALL FIVE road types: off-network 1 beside on-network 2, 3, 4 and 5. 729 rows = running exhaust on five road types x 125 cohorts + start exhaust on road type 1 x 104.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES, which §23 asks for before a dimension is called covered (PLAN.md §7.3.46, conventions §101, §102).\n\n* THE ROAD TYPE AS AN AXIS. Every other RunSpec here selects one on-network road type, so a running-exhaust rate was computed on exactly one (`run_roadTypeID` over `run_rows`, which summed this run's four to 14 and joined no link). Here running energy is computed on four, each with its own VMT share, `zoneRoadType` SHO allocation, average-speed distribution and drive-schedule brackets -- 51.09, 62.82, 240.73 and 303.73 on road types 2 to 5 -- and the road-type-independent part is checked from the other side: the road-4 block equals `expand-counties`' Washtenaw block cell for cell. A rate or an activity read at the wrong road type, or a self-join of rate rows that forgot the road type, moves four blocks against each other here and nowhere else.\n\n* OFF-NETWORK IDLE, A SUM ACROSS THAT AXIS. Running exhaust on road type 1 is TotalActivityGenerator step 190c: per age, SHO(1) = max(S (tif - SD/S) / (1 - tif), 0) from the four on-network SHO values, BaseRateGenerator's driving-idle fraction per road type (0.00505, 0.05721, 0.03030, 0.12842) and `totalIdleFraction` at Michigan's idle region 103, county type 1 (0.245044679), at the idle mode's rate alone. 31.31 of energy, every cell within 8e-06.\n\n* A RAGGED BLOCK SET. Six output blocks of two pollutant-processes: running on five road types, start on one, so a block is a (pollutant-process, road type) pair and `outputPolProcessCount` is 6.\n\n729 of 729 on the promotion's first run, key set exact, worst cell 1.009e-05, per-pollutant sum 6.3e-07. `n_outputRate` is bound to 729, the number the chain recomputes as `rateSurvivorCount`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-roadtypes"
    ]
  },
